    <string name="desk_title">Subscriptions desk</string>
    <string name="desk_intro">Feeds the paper has noticed something about. Nothing here happens on its own, and a dismissed note stays away for six months.</string>
    <string name="desk_healthy_title">All in order</string>
    <string name="desk_healthy_detail">Every feed is being delivered and nothing needs your attention.</string>
    <string name="desk_flag_broken">Not arriving</string>
    <string name="desk_flag_moved">Changed address</string>
    <string name="desk_flag_quiet">Gone quiet</string>
    <string name="desk_flag_ignored">Never opened</string>
    <string name="desk_flag_noisy">Posts a lot, read a little</string>
    <string name="desk_flag_loved">Read cover to cover</string>
    <string name="desk_about_broken">These could not be fetched for a week or more. The usual alternative addresses were tried as well and none of them answered with a feed.</string>
    <string name="desk_about_moved">These were found at a new address, which is now the one in use. There is nothing you need to do.</string>
    <string name="desk_about_quiet">No posts in 90 days. That is not a problem: they are kept, checked less often, and return to the paper when they post again.</string>
    <string name="desk_about_ignored">These have run in ten or more editions over the last two months without one of their stories being opened.</string>
    <string name="desk_about_noisy">Thirty or more posts a week, and almost none of them opened.</string>
    <string name="desk_about_loved">You read most of what these publish and Like it often. As a favourite, a feed is always given room.</string>
